cartridge "SPACE HUNT/ANTHONY WOOD/1984"
' SPACE HUNT
' Based on "Space Hunt" by Anthony Wood, Ahoy! April 1985 (Commodore 64
' BASIC, 34 blocks on the disk; "(C) COPYRIGHT 1984 ANTHONY WOOD", dated
' 6/18/84 in its REMs), for the ColecoVision in Amy by Amy Bienvenu; this
' version by Claude (Anthropic).
'
' A text adventure: from an old lunar space station, find the pressure
' suit, the code and the blaster, fly the space ship to an asteroid and
' dig out the fabulous treasure. Not a cell-for-cell port: the listing's
' rooms, things, words and rules on a ColecoVision screen.
'
' Screen: a picture of the place on rows 1-7 (the top screen third as a
' bitmap: names 0-255, its own patterns and colours), the explorer walking
' in it as sprites, the place's name in gold on row 8, the room text on
' rows 9-14 (MORE on row 15 when it runs over), a divider on row 15, the
' answers on rows 16-19 (MORE on row 22), what you carry as icons on rows
' 20-21, a hint on row 22.
'
' Controls (either joystick): push the stick north, south, east or west to
' walk (a fresh push a step). Left button: the command list (LOOK,
' INVENTORY, EXAMINE, GET, DROP, OPEN, UNLOCK, USE, WEAR, READ, PUSH, GO,
' TYPE, UNSCREW, SHOOT, MOVE, LIE DOWN, SAVE, LOAD, QUIT): the stick
' chooses, left button takes it, right button closes the list. A command
' that needs a thing then lists the things here and carried. TYPE shows
' four digits set with the stick. A button turns a MORE page. Keypad not
' used.
'
' The listing's rules are kept: its 14 rooms and exits (DATA 2450-2630),
' the space ship also seen from the asteroid plain (line 220), every
' thing and where it lies, every answer and the order of its checks
' (lines 400-1980), the hidden key, screw driver, panel, note, suit and
' blaster, the locker wired to 10,000 volts (open it in the suit), the
' airlock button (cycles the doors; deadly without the suit), the suit
' dropped outside, the code typed on the control board (any code starting
' 321, as LEFT$(N$,3) tests it; the ship flies once), the boulder shot only
' while lying down (moving stands you up again), and the treasure taken to
' win.
'
' Liberties taken:
' - The stick and command lists instead of typed words: the listing's
'   synonyms (N, NORTH, GET/TAKE/PICK, PRESS/PUSH, BLAST/SHOOT...) become
'   one entry each; FIRE is left out (it only answered "TRY SHOOT").
'   A thing is chosen from the things here and carried, so "I DON'T
'   UNDERSTAND" for unknown words cannot happen; the listing's quirk that
'   "EQUIPMENT LOCKER" typed in full meant the engine room's equipment is
'   gone too.
' - The red button can't be taken (the listing let you carry it and press
'   it anywhere, which rewired the exits of whatever room you stood in).
' - SAVE and LOAD keep one game in video memory until the power goes off
'   (the listing saved to disk).
' - QUIT asks first and goes back to the title.
' - Spelling: PANEL (the listing has PANNEL), "HIT BY ROCKS" (HIT HIT).
' - Pictures, the explorer as sprites (in a jumpsuit, or in the pressure
'   suit once worn), icons of what you carry, sparks, a blast, the take-off,
'   a title tune and sound.
'
' House rules: tiles from code 128 (icons 128-155, divider 156, pointer
' 157, digit box 158, gold letters 192-255 made from the font at start-up),
' the tune once (quieter than the effects), NMI off while drawing,
' `set sprite count 4` again after every `clear sprites`, nothing flashes
' faster than 3 Hz.

